description: 'Implement actor join primitive (review 12_safety; P1-16 area). Current
  state: *main epilogue joins workers implicitly (actor_processes_then_stops test);
  there is NO user-facing join — grep shows no `join` keyword in lexer/parser. Programs
  cannot wait for a specific actor to finish mid-program. Deliverable: `join {actor}`
  (or design-approved prose surface) that parks the caller coroutine until the target
  actor''s mailbox is closed and handler loop exits; must compose with stop/close
  semantics in docs/concurrency.md. Definition of done: parser+typer+codegen+runtime
  support; conformance tests incl. join-after-stop, join-twice, join-self-deadlock
  diagnostic if detectable.'
